-<a name="id96814"></a><h2>Description</h2>
+<a name="id93853"></a><h2>Description</h2>
 <p>All settings are presented as a number of named parameters divided into named sections. The parameters values are stored as strings. Individual parameters may be queried via subscript operators, like this:</p>
 <p><code class="computeroutput"><pre class="programlisting">
 <span class="identifier">optional</span><span class="special">&lt;</span> <span class="identifier">string</span> <span class="special">&gt;</span> <span class="identifier">param</span> <span class="special">=</span> <span class="identifier">settings</span><span class="special">[</span><span class="string">"Section1"</span><span class="special">]</span><span class="special">[</span><span class="string">"Param1"</span><span class="special">]</span><span class="special">;</span> <span class="comment">// reads parameter "Param1" in section "Section1"</span>
@@ -52,8 +52,8 @@
 </pre></code></p>
 <p>There are also other methods to work with parameters. </p>
